 "notes": "Envelope (pointwise minimum) of the blue (2s1/2-2p1/2 Lamb shift, DeltaM*=2e-10 eV at 2 sigma) and green (1s1/2-2s1/2 renormalised with 2s1/2-8s1/2) hydrogen bounds in Fig. 3 (combinedhydrogen.eps), which the paper states are 'the best ones that we can derive from atomic spectra' and combines in the Fig. 1 summary. Curves extracted by color thresholding of the 600 dpi raster EPS with axis calibration from major ticks (x: Log10 m/eV = 0..12, y: Log10 chi = 0..-8). He+ Lamb-shift bound (Fig. 4, Z=2) checked and never dips below the hydrogen envelope. Below 1 eV (Fig. 3 left edge) the curve is extended with the chi ~ 1/m slope of the same-n/renormalised bound, consistent with Fig. 1 where the dotted black line reaches chi=1 at m ~ 10^-2.5 eV. Bounds quoted at 2 sigma (95% CL). Not a dark-matter search; no rho_DM dependence.",
